pendencies":[],"digest":"3d2dc75530327f5e4ed04263a34f96d1065bc0b71a07a7339796192b2afd68e1"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:E4","usage":{"input_tokens":235876,"output_tokens":3439,"requests":6}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"37e9ba1d1363208a1a6126ad1dc193e135ce72dc3ceb90125b7214ed24d3562d"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":73018,"output_tokens":3865,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"6c3354cab2f4612b515b90bfdf75648612a0d660d327171ba22f81604be828f6"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T1","usage":{"input_tokens":71188,"output_tokens":1795,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"3a0bcd483355bdba66da40b662a1dac6b191b5e568575fd4bb55c385c8e605fb"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":78551,"output_tokens":1583,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"c53adaf505bec0b494b7cd78bf86b6b941e5dfd70129137e8c325f7e789a2123"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":67301,"output_tokens":1800,"requests":4}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State explicitly where the empty-scope fail-closed guard lives (e.g. `_apply_staged_files` returns 0 immediately when `scope` is empty, before iterating), so the 'no file copied back on empty scope' guarantee cannot be defeated by `in_repair_scope`'s empty-scope default.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'An empty scope is fail-closed. When the failure summary names no parseable path, no file is copied back and the repair degrades to agent repair.'","Plan: '`in_repair_scope` tests each changed file against them.'","A per-file predicate over an empty scope must return either always-true (fail-open, copies the whole tree) or always-false; the plan asserts the fail-closed outcome but locates the guard in a per-file tester whose empty-scope default is unstated.","This is the ticket's core defect ('it is unscoped, so it rewrites the whole tree'), so a fail-open empty scope silently reintroduces it."],"finding":"The plan's 'empty scope is fail-closed' guarantee is not achieved by the two mechanisms it names (`in_repair_scope` + `_apply_staged_files`); a per-file scope tester on an empty scope naturally matches everything (fail-open), the exact whole-tree rewrite the ticket removes. The plan does not specify where the empty-scope short-circuit lives.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb7f95fe927dd6fd8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Bounding what a fix may write back'","norm_id":"ne0f3e7122a38c7fd","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A prettier failure whose summary is `[warn] Code style issues found in the above file(s).` names no path, producing an empty scope; the fix command reformats every file it is pointed at."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Specify that `_apply_staged_files` short-circuits to 0 when `failing_files` yields an empty tuple, independent of `in_repair_scope`'s per-file result, and add a test asserting an empty scope copies zero files even when the fix changed files.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify the discriminators `_project_autofix` reads to name each of the six outcomes (e.g. distinguish empty-scope from path-rejected using `failing_files(...)==()` vs `applied==0 and scope`, and non-zero-exit from pod-failure via `run_fix` exit code vs a raised `PodEngineError`), so every declared outcome is derivable from the return/exception surface.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: '`_project_autofix` emits a structured log naming which path it took, one of `applied`, `no-fix-command`, `fix-exited-non-zero`, `pod-failed`, `empty-scope`, or `path-rejected`.'","Plan describes `run_fix` verifying and `_apply_staged_files` copying, but does not specify what fields `_project_autofix` reads to name `empty-scope` (no scope paths) apart from `path-rejected` (scope paths present, none matched) or `fix-exited-non-zero` apart from `pod-failed`.","The motivating incident was invisibility ('llm_calls=0 on every attempt, so no agent ever saw the failure'), so a lossy outcome label defeats the stated purpose of this section."],"finding":"The plan commits `_project_autofix` to emitting one of six named outcomes, but the described data flow (a `verified` bool from `run_fix` plus an int count from `_apply_staged_files`) cannot distinguish all six: `empty-scope` and `path-rejected` both surface as zero applied, and `fix-exited-non-zero` vs `pod-failed` are not separable from a single `verified` bool.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcc5c19933e015239","impact":1.0,"i