.py gains gate_engine_privileged; gates/pod_runner.py gains a privileged flag","norm_id":"n0ed6ec3d3252c854","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor defaults gate_engine_privileged to true and every check pod silently runs privileged.","An executor defaults it to false and the fix path never gets the privilege buildah needs."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Document gate_engine_privileged's default (e.g. false) and scope the privileged flag to the copy-out/fix invocation so check runs stay unprivileged.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the fix_command value shape (shell string vs argv list) mirroring how existing check commands are declared, and note it in config/local/checks.yaml.example.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'services/orchestration/checks/config.py parses the new fix_command key.'","Absence: no stated type/format for fix_command; examples like 'ruff', 'prettier --write', 'make fix' vary between single-token and multi-token forms."],"finding":"The shape of the fix_command config value is not specified — whether it is a shell string, an argv list, or a script — which the config parser and the fix script builder both depend on.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9c26ad5a88b8f7b4","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: services/orchestration/checks/config.py parses the new fix_command key","norm_id":"n7991e05c7b8d5f39","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Parser treats fix_command as a bare string but the builder expects a list, or vice versa.","A multi-word command like 'prettier --write' is mis-split."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Declare fix_command as a shell string executed in the pod, matching the existing check-command convention, and show the exact form in checks.yaml.example.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Capture the privileged-pod rationale and probe evidence in an ADR or AGENTS.md/design-doc update alongside the pod_runner change.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'gates/pod_runner.py gains a privileged flag ... because buildah cannot unpack a layer unprivileged under k3s.'","'Four probe pods confirmed that CAP_SYS_ADMIN alone ... both fail.'","Absence: Scope lists code + config + tests but no design-doc/ADR entry for the privileged-execution decision."],"finding":"Introducing privileged pod execution under k3s is a novel, security-relevant architectural decision, but no ADR / AGENTS.md / design-doc update is listed to capture why buildah needs privileged and what the blast radius is.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb28b53f2defef008","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Grounded assumptions: 'Buildah requires privileged: true under k3s on Colima.'","norm_id":"nf62002f2f6ff68f5","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future maintainer sees privileged pods and cannot find the rationale or the probe evidence."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that the project fix command runs under a bounded timeout in the pod, and that a timeout degrades to agent repair (with a distinct outcome log value).","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["The plan reuses the check transport ('reuses that transport') but does not state whether the fix command inherits the check runner's timeout or has its own bound.","Fix command is project-declared and arbitrary ('ruff', 'prettier --write', 'gofmt', or a bespoke `make fix`)."],"finding":"The plan does not state that the project-declared fix command runs under a timeout when executed in the pod. A malicious or runaway fix command (e.g. a project-declared `npm run lint:fix` that hangs on a prompt) could block the repair activity indefinitely.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f03755b81f422fe8d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / runner.py run_fix; gates/pod_runner.py","norm_id":"n1af85051d5e3afe6","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A project declares a fix_command that hangs or waits on stdin; the repair activity blocks with no timeout-driven degrade to agent repair."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Note that `run_fix` inherits the check runner's pod execution timeout and that a timed-out fix is treated like `pod-failed`/`fix-exited-non-zero`, emitting an outcome log and falling through to agent repair.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impac